---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import HarnessesNav from '../../components/harnesses/HarnessesNav.astro';
import HarnessCard from '../../components/harnesses/HarnessCard.astro';
import { CATEGORY_COPY, harnessesByCategory } from '../../lib/harnesses';
import { harnesses } from '../../lib/harnesses-data';

const copy = CATEGORY_COPY.agent;
const rows = harnessesByCategory(harnesses(), 'agent');
---

<Base title={copy.label} description={copy.lede}>
  <main id="main" class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-10 sm:px-6">
    <HarnessesNav current="agents" />
    <h1 class="display mt-6 text-4xl sm:text-5xl">{copy.label}</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">{copy.lede}</p>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-muted">
      Hermes is amdai’s daily setup on local-desktop. Shannon (@iamMrDuncan) describes a multi-profile
      Hermes setup and Hermes desktop bot mode beside that house path —
      <a class="underline decoration-accent/40" href="/labs/shannon">cited, not measured by AMDai</a>.
      Herdr and Coolify are cataloged from the same write-up; they are not
      <code>/v1</code> chat clients and are not used on our rig. Claude Code and Codex CLI attach
      only where the local server implements their native APIs (Anthropic Messages / OpenAI
      Responses) — not a drop-in <code>/v1/chat/completions</code> assumption. Cursor’s override
      is not a first-class localhost path. OpenAI-style tools and structured JSON on
      llama-server are on
      <a class="underline decoration-accent/40" href="/guides/tool-calling">tool calling</a>.
    </p>
    <ul class="mt-8 grid gap-3">
      {rows.map((row) => (
        <li>
          <HarnessCard row={row} />
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </main>
</Base>
